  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the minimum probability of each lottery and prefers the one with the smaller minimum probability. In this case, Lottery B has a minimum probability of 20% (for 4000 Euros), which is lower than Lottery A’s 25% (for 3000 Euros), so the reason would select B. The individual also refers to accepting the 'lower probability' to 'win more', which aligns with preferring Lottery B due to its lower chance (20%) of the higher outcome. The individual considers the probabilities and outcomes in a way that matches the core logic of the decision reason: comparing the smallest probabilities associated with the positive outcomes and being willing to accept that lower probability for a higher reward. Although the individual's justification includes a motivational element ('more to win'), the key informational focus—comparing the low probabilities of winning and favoring the lower one when tied to a higher prize—matches the structure of the decision reason. Thus, the relevant information (minimum probabilities) is considered, and the rule (prefer lower minimum probability) is implicitly followed in the justification.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

